              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ganita Prakash | Grade 8"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.089,
            0.289,
            0.112
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Trapezium"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.12,
            0.577,
            0.232
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Parallelograms are quadrilaterals that have parallel opposite sides. We get a new type of quadrilateral if we relax this condition. "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Trapezium:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " A trapezium is a quadrilateral with at least one pair of parallel opposite sides."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.585,
            0.108,
            0.913,
            0.228
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 3,
              "bbox": [
                0.585,
                0.108,
                0.913,
                0.228
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_24_image_3.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.243,
            0.846,
            0.265
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ Construct a trapezium. Measure the base angles (marked in the figure)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.277,
            0.757,
            0.324
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ Can you find the remaining angles without measuring them? Since PQ||SR, we have"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.334,
            0.62,
            0.355
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Property 1:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle S + \\angle P = 180^{\\circ}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle \\mathrm{R} + \\angle Q = 180^{\\circ}"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.358,
            0.848,
            0.396
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Using these facts, the remaining angles can easily be found. Verify your answer after finding them."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.4,
            0.847,
            0.439
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "When the non-parallel sides of a trapezium have the same lengths, the trapezium is called an "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "isosceles trapezium.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.448,
            0.605,
            0.471
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ How do we construct an isosceles trapezium?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.483,
            0.831,
            0.507
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ Construct an isosceles trapezium UVWX, with UV||XW. Measure ∠U."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.162,
            0.517,
            0.498,
            0.665
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 11,
              "bbox": [
                0.162,
                0.517,
                0.498,
                0.665
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_24_image_11.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.537,
            0.518,
            0.842,
            0.641
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 12,
              "bbox": [
                0.537,
                0.518,
                0.842,
                0.641
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_24_image_12.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.681,
            0.757,
            0.701
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Can you find the remaining angles without measuring them?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.705,
            0.847,
            0.762
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Does it appear that the angles opposite to the equal sides—∠U and ∠V—are also equal? Can we find congruent triangles here? Consider line segments XY and WZ perpendicular to UV."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.763,
            0.512,
            0.786
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "What type of quadrilateral is XWZY?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.79,
            0.564,
            0.904
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Since XW||UV, "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "a = 180^{\\circ} - \\angle XYZ = 90^{\\circ},"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "b = 180^{\\circ} - \\angle WZY  = 90^{\\circ}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " (since the internal angles on the same side of a transversal add up to 180°) Hence, XWZY is a rectangle."
            }
          ]
        },
